No way.

255
00:12:04,959 --> 00:12:06,792
She won't be
getting up for a while.

256
00:12:06,875 --> 00:12:08,124
I hurt her pretty good.

257
00:12:08,208 --> 00:12:08,833
(Mai Zenin gasps)

258
00:12:08,917 --> 00:12:12,040
What's this? A challenge?

259
00:12:13,415 --> 00:12:15,958
(both grunting)

260
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,082
Nice support, Maki!

261
00:12:19,707 --> 00:12:21,874
You put a bunch of holes
in my brand new tracksuit.

262
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:24,498
I oughta rip this rag off you

263
00:12:24,581 --> 00:12:26,998
and use it to make it
my own summer uniform.

264
00:12:27,081 --> 00:12:30,665
Next time I'll put the
holes in your body instead.

265
00:12:30,748 --> 00:12:32,581
Plus, you can't wear this

266
00:12:32,665 --> 00:12:34,288
with those stick
legs of (groans).

267
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:39,163
[Nobara Kugisaki]
Just shut your mouth.

268
00:12:39,247 --> 00:12:40,847
[Aoi Toudou] Come
on, Mai, we're leaving.

269
00:12:40,914 --> 00:12:42,154
[Nobara Kugisaki] What? No way.

270
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:45,871
Oh, there's my jacket.

271
00:12:45,955 --> 00:12:48,537
Where's Fushiguro?

272
00:12:48,621 --> 00:12:51,746
Don't worry, he's fine.
He's out with the others.

273
00:12:51,829 --> 00:12:53,829
Looks like you're having fun.

274
00:12:53,913 --> 00:12:54,996
(panting) I am,

275
00:12:55,079 --> 00:12:56,995
but I'm just
getting started here.

276
00:12:57,078 --> 00:12:58,870
No, you're not.

277
00:12:58,954 --> 00:12:59,745
Unlike you, I still have
important business

278
00:12:59,828 --> 00:13:02,453
to attend to here in Tokyo.

279
00:13:02,954 --> 00:13:06,202
My personal handshake

280
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:07,869
and it's with Takada!

281
00:13:11,619 --> 00:13:12,702
[All] Huh?

282
00:13:16,202 --> 00:13:18,952
Who knows what I might
do if I don't catch that train

283
00:13:19,034 --> 00:13:21,576
and I can't make it
to the hall on time.

284
00:13:22,326 --> 00:13:24,034
Come on, Mai, let's go.

285
00:13:24,117 --> 00:13:26,910
[Mai Zenin] (grunts)
You're so selfish.

286
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:29,867
[Aoi Toudou] I still can't
believe I lost the lottery

287
00:13:29,951 --> 00:13:31,700
for the one in Kyoto.

288
00:13:31,784 --> 00:13:32,867
As for you,

289
00:13:32,951 --> 00:13:35,408
you won't get off this
easy at the Exchange Event.

290
00:13:35,492 --> 00:13:37,242
Quit acting like you
beat me, damn it,

291
00:13:37,325 --> 00:13:38,825
and gimme that uniform now!

292
00:13:38,909 --> 00:13:41,241
Cut it out, you idiot.

293
00:13:41,324 --> 00:13:43,866
Winning or losing a fight
here doesn't mean a thing.

294
00:13:43,950 --> 00:13:45,908
Save that up for
the Exchange Event.

295
00:13:47,491 --> 00:13:49,407
Maki, is Mai right?

296
00:13:49,491 --> 00:13:52,406
She said you don't
have Cursed Energy.

297
00:13:52,490 --> 00:13:53,782
Yes, that's true.

298
00:13:53,865 --> 00:13:54,949
In fact,

299
00:13:55,907 --> 00:13:57,990
I need these to even see Curses.

300
00:13:59,907 --> 00:14:00,966
That's why I use Cursed Tools.

301
00:14:00,990 --> 00:14:02,989
They already have
Curses imbued in them.

302
00:14:04,697 --> 00:14:05,882
I can't pour my own
Cursed Energy into them

303
00:14:05,906 --> 00:14:08,572
to do things like you all do.

304
00:14:08,989 --> 00:14:11,280
Oh.

305
00:14:11,364 --> 00:14:13,029
Like that thing
Gojo gave Itadori.

306
00:14:15,821 --> 00:14:17,613
Then why be a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

307
00:14:18,988 --> 00:14:20,404
To spite my family.

308
00:14:21,863 --> 00:14:23,445
I can't wait to see their faces

309
00:14:23,528 --> 00:14:24,820
when I become a
bigshot sorcerer.

310
00:14:24,904 --> 00:14:29,820
After all, they've looked
down on me all these years.

311
00:14:31,362 --> 00:14:32,278
Come on.

312
00:14:32,362 --> 00:14:33,987
Let's hurry over and see Shoko.

313
00:14:36,945 --> 00:14:40,778
[Nobara Kugisaki] You know,
I really respect you, Maki.

314
00:14:40,861 --> 00:14:41,945
[Maki Zenin] Is that so?

315
00:14:44,110 --> 00:14:47,193
(upbeat theme music)

316
00:14:49,777 --> 00:14:51,985
(upbeat theme music)

317
00:14:54,109 --> 00:14:57,317
(river babbling)

318
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,150
(birds chirping)

319
00:15:05,108 --> 00:15:07,775
Why is Yaga still not here?

320
00:15:07,858 --> 00:15:09,107
Time is a precious thing

321
00:15:09,191 --> 00:15:11,858
to an old man who's
coming ever closer to death.

322
00:15:15,858 --> 00:15:17,538
[Satoru Gojo] I'm
sorry, but Principal Yaga

323
00:15:17,608 --> 00:15:19,523
won't be here for a while yet.

324
00:15:19,607 --> 00:15:20,649
Oh?

325
00:15:23,607 --> 00:15:26,148
Somehow, the schedule
he was given was incorrect.

326
00:15:26,232 --> 00:15:28,982
After some threats to Ijichi.

327
00:15:30,439 --> 00:15:33,689
Thank you for the other
day, Principal Gakuganji.

328
00:15:33,773 --> 00:15:36,314
Sorry? What day
are you referring to?

329
00:15:36,397 --> 00:15:38,356
Don't play dumb
with me, old man.

330
00:15:38,439 --> 00:15:40,813
I'm talking about Yuji Itadori.

331
00:15:40,897 --> 00:15:43,813
As head of the conservatives
you were involved too, right?

332
00:15:44,605 --> 00:15:45,146
My goodness.

333
00:15:45,230 --> 00:15:47,563
Youth these days.

334
00:15:47,647 --> 00:15:49,521
Have you no manners anymore?

335
00:15:49,605 --> 00:15:52,145
Have you lost all
respect for your elders?

336
00:15:52,229 --> 00:15:54,687
I never had any respect
for you to start with.

337
00:15:54,771 --> 00:15:56,354
Elders like you love
to act important

338
00:15:56,437 --> 00:15:58,604
and frankly it just sucks.

339
00:15:58,687 --> 00:15:59,687
[Kasumi Miwa] Watch it!

340
00:15:59,729 --> 00:16:00,604
[Satoru Gojo] Hm?

341
00:16:00,687 --> 00:16:03,019
Your conduct is unacceptable.

342
00:16:03,102 --> 00:16:06,394
Stop it, or I'll report you
to the proper authorities.

343
00:16:06,478 --> 00:16:07,561
Oh, wow!

344
00:16:07,645 --> 00:16:11,561
It's Satoru Gojo in-person
sitting right in front of me!

345
00:16:11,645 --> 00:16:13,019
Knock yourself out.

346
00:16:13,102 --> 00:16:15,727
I don't plan to
chat for very long.

347
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:17,101
(Kasumi Miwa grumbling)

348
00:16:17,185 --> 00:16:20,310
[Kasumi Miwa] (giggling) He
spoke to me, he spoke to me!

349
00:16:21,977 --> 00:16:23,560
[Satoru Gojo] Last
night, I was attacked

350
00:16:23,644 --> 00:16:26,226
by two unregistered
Special Grade Cursed Spirits.

351
00:16:26,309 --> 00:16:27,601
Oh?

352
00:16:27,684 --> 00:16:29,226
Well, that is very unfortunate.

353
00:16:30,267 --> 00:16:31,935
Don't get me wrong here.

354
00:16:32,017 --> 00:16:33,559
It was about as much trouble

355
00:16:33,643 --> 00:16:36,016
as answering a sidewalk survey.

356
00:16:36,099 --> 00:16:38,934
[Kasumi Miwa] (moaning) So cool!

357
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:43,141
These two Cursed Spirits
were capable of communication,

358
00:16:43,225 --> 00:16:45,975
and they probably have
allies who are just as strong.

359
00:16:48,182 --> 00:16:50,098
And it's not just our foes.

360
00:16:50,182 --> 00:16:53,349
Hakari, Okkotsu,
and your Toudou.

361
00:16:54,682 --> 00:16:56,807
In recent years, the
quality level of our students

362
00:16:56,891 --> 00:16:58,556
has risen dramatically as well.

363
00:16:59,181 --> 00:17:02,348
Then there was last year's
incident with Suguru Geto.

364
00:17:06,514 --> 00:17:09,138
And now, the appearance
of Sukuna's vessel.

365
00:17:10,055 --> 00:17:12,764
What are you trying to say?

366
00:17:12,847 --> 00:17:14,597
You're still not getting this?

367
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:17,430
The wave of power you guys
have been trying to hold back

368
00:17:17,513 --> 00:17:20,054
with your pointless
status and traditions

369
00:17:20,137 --> 00:17:20,971
has grown bigger
than you can handle

370
00:17:21,054 --> 00:17:23,679
and is now descending upon us.

371
00:17:23,763 --> 00:17:25,930
You won't be able to
measure the coming age

372
00:17:26,012 --> 00:17:28,471
with just the classification
of Special Grade.

373
00:17:28,554 --> 00:17:29,721
And if you really believe

374
00:17:29,804 --> 00:17:31,929
I'm the only one
who's gonna fight back,

375
00:17:32,011 --> 00:17:34,386
you're gonna wind
up hurt, old man.

376
00:17:35,511 --> 00:17:36,511
I think

377
00:17:37,511 --> 00:17:39,553
that you're way out
of line, young man.

378
00:17:40,553 --> 00:17:42,219
Oh, I'm scared.

379
00:17:42,302 --> 00:17:45,469
Well, I've said all I wanted
to say, so I'll be going now.

380
00:17:48,928 --> 00:17:50,636
(Kasumi Miwa grumbles)

381
00:17:50,719 --> 00:17:52,260
Oh, and Principal
Yaga will be along

382
00:17:52,344 --> 00:17:53,468
in a couple of hours.

383
00:17:53,551 --> 00:17:55,092
Later!

384
00:17:55,176 --> 00:17:57,218
[Kasumi Miwa] A couple of hours?

385
00:17:59,885 --> 00:18:01,426
(Yoshinobu Gakuganji sighs)

386
00:18:01,509 --> 00:18:04,217
Miwa, would you
find me some tea?

387
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,342
Yes.

388
00:18:08,550 --> 00:18:09,550
I'll be right back.

389
00:18:12,383 --> 00:18:14,258
(Kasumi Miwa giggling)

390
00:18:14,342 --> 00:18:15,216
If I can catch up to him,

391
00:18:15,299 --> 00:18:18,674
maybe I can get him to
take a picture with me!

392
00:18:18,758 --> 00:18:23,507
-(bright music)
-(crowd chattering)

393
00:18:23,591 --> 00:18:25,216
Taka-tan Beam,
if you don't mind.

394
00:18:26,131 --> 00:18:28,757
Awe! I'm happy to!

395
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,048
Tan, Taka-tan!

396
00:18:33,757 --> 00:18:35,357
-(Aoi Toudou gasping)
-(crowd chattering)

397
00:18:35,381 --> 00:18:38,339
[Worker] Time's up, pal.

398
00:18:53,338 --> 00:18:56,463
(serene piano music)

399
00:19:32,292 --> 00:19:33,375
Excuse me.

400
00:19:36,292 --> 00:19:37,292
Did you do that

401
00:19:39,626 --> 00:19:40,626
inside the theater?

402
00:19:42,666 --> 00:19:44,124
(Mahito chuckles)

403
00:19:44,208 --> 00:19:46,541
Wow,

404
00:19:46,625 --> 00:19:49,208
so you can actually see me.

405
00:19:49,291 --> 00:19:52,124
(ominous music)

406
00:20:01,123 --> 00:20:02,916
(rain pouring)

407
00:20:02,998 --> 00:20:04,248
It's a gruesome sight.

408
00:20:05,372 --> 00:20:07,706
Are you ready to
witness it, Itadori?

409
00:20:11,915 --> 00:20:15,164
(Yuji Itadori grunts)

410
00:20:19,872 --> 00:20:22,330
(Closing Theme Music)

411
00:20:26,913 --> 00:20:30,704
(singing in Japanese)

412
00:21:50,113 --> 00:21:53,363
[Kasumi Miwa] (giggling)
Thank you so much!

413
00:21:53,447 --> 00:21:56,404
[Satoru Gojo] Oh,
it's my pleasure.

414
00:21:56,487 --> 00:21:58,404
[Kasumi Miwa] (giggling)
I got a photo with him!

415
00:22:11,570 --> 00:22:13,653
My tea?

416
00:22:13,737 --> 00:22:14,778
(Kasumi Miwa gasps)

417
00:22:15,986 --> 00:22:17,027
[Announcers] Juju Stroll!

418
00:22:17,819 --> 00:22:20,736
(crowd chattering)

419
00:22:20,819 --> 00:22:21,694
[Fan] Man, she's hot,

420
00:22:21,777 --> 00:22:23,378
but she's staring at
us like we're garbage.

421
00:22:23,402 --> 00:22:25,277
[Fan] Stop looking at her!

422
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:26,527
Mai, sorry to be so long.

423
00:22:26,611 --> 00:22:27,527
What's wrong?

424
00:22:27,610 --> 00:22:29,735
Did something happen
while I was gone?

425
00:22:29,818 --> 00:22:30,318
[Mai Zenin] Aside
from having to come

426
00:22:30,401 --> 00:22:31,526
to this stupid event?

427
00:22:31,610 --> 00:22:33,401
[Aoi Toudou] So this
moment has finally come.

428
00:22:33,484 --> 00:22:34,484
Huh?

429
00:22:35,401 --> 00:22:36,443
What's this?

430
00:22:36,526 --> 00:22:39,066
[Aoi Toudou] For the
next handshake event.

431
00:22:39,150 --> 00:22:41,692
You should go experience how
wonderful Takada is in-person.

432
00:22:41,775 --> 00:22:43,734
[Mai Zenin] This is
just plain annoying.

433
00:22:43,817 --> 00:22:45,942
[Aoi Toudou] This
is my duty as a fan,

434
00:22:46,025 --> 00:22:47,734
and as her future husband.

435
00:22:47,817 --> 00:22:49,691
[Mai Zenin] And
that's just plain creepy,

436
00:22:49,774 --> 00:22:50,524
but if I reject his offer,

437
00:22:50,608 --> 00:22:53,900
he'll just get even
more annoying.

438
00:22:53,982 --> 00:22:54,858
What's the matter?

439
00:22:54,941 --> 00:22:57,399
-(high-spirited music)
-(crowd chattering)

440
00:22:57,482 --> 00:22:59,941
(detector beeping)

441
00:23:00,024 --> 00:23:01,481
Oh. Yeah, sure.

442
00:23:02,857 --> 00:23:05,481
(worker gasping)

443
00:23:05,565 --> 00:23:06,773
[Takada] Wow, a girl!

444
00:23:06,857 --> 00:23:08,981
Is this your first time
coming to see me?

445
00:23:09,064 --> 00:23:10,607
Yeah.

446
00:23:10,690 --> 00:23:11,356
[Takada] What's your name?

447
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,564
[Mai Zenin] Mai.

448
00:23:13,647 --> 00:23:15,980
[Takada] (giggling)
Mai, are you tired?

449
00:23:16,063 --> 00:23:17,939
Did you have to
wait in line long?

450
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:20,731
[Mai Zenin] It was more the
people than the line really.

451
00:23:20,814 --> 00:23:23,938
Then come back again
when you're feeling better.

452
00:23:24,021 --> 00:23:26,104
I won't forget you ever, Mai.

453
00:23:26,646 --> 00:23:29,313
[Aoi Toudou] Ah,
Mai, you're back.

454
00:23:29,396 --> 00:23:30,979
How was it?

455
00:23:31,062 --> 00:23:32,229
[Mai Zenin] Fine.

456
00:23:32,313 --> 00:23:34,103
Yeah, I get it.

457
00:23:34,187 --> 00:23:35,395
Takada is the kind of woman

458
00:23:35,478 --> 00:23:37,812
who's difficult to
describe in mere words.

459
00:23:39,896 --> 00:23:43,645
[Mai Zenin] (inhales)
She's not bad. (sighs)

460
00:23:44,437 --> 00:23:47,561
(upbeat theme music)

